---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript';
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS vs Postscript: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Plan the move from retired Yotpo messaging to Postscript SMS, with a separate email owner and explicit Reviews and Loyalty handoffs.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Yotpo messaging remain the email half of this stack?",
    "answer": "Do not plan around inactive messaging. Assign email journeys to a working email system; retained Reviews and Loyalty are separate products and responsibilities."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will the Yotpo Loyalty connector recover old SMS subscribers?",
    "answer": "The documented connector references reward points in SMS automations. It is not a subscriber recovery or retired-dashboard export promise."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is Postscript worth evaluating?",
    "answer": "Evaluate it when you need an SMS destination and can staff capture, replies and suppression. Confirm your required countries, import eligibility and workflows with the vendor instead of using a revenue-share cutoff."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should the first send be approved internally?",
    "answer": "Reconcile eligible records and opt-outs, check links and stop events on staff profiles, assign replies and document the pause action. Start only with the segment whose permission and message purpose you can substantiate."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="link" href="/compare">← Comparisons</a>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Migration decision</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">This is now a migration decision. Yotpo messaging is no longer an operating alternative to Postscript. Start with the SMS jobs you need to restore, the consent records you already hold, and the email platform that will own everything outside the text program.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Start with the service that actually exists</h2>
        <p>Yotpo’s <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/integrations">live decommission notice</a> says its SMS application has ended and its dashboard and background services are inactive. Do not schedule a side-by-side trial or assume a new export can be obtained there. Inventory files already retained, Shopify records and your other systems; ask support about missing records without promising their recovery.</p>
        <h2>Postscript is the SMS destination in this plan</h2>
        <p>A text-channel migration does not assign email ownership. Write a trigger register with columns for capture source, consent evidence, destination, stop event and reply owner. Welcome email, receipts and email winback need their own named systems. A review request should also have one owner even when an SMS reminder accompanies it. Missing email journeys are a migration gap, rather than a reason to keep inactive Yotpo messaging.</p>
        <h2>Reconstruct permission before importing a phone number</h2>
        <p>Separate existing SMS permission from email permission and from order contact details. Keep the original source, timestamp and disclosure where available, plus opt-outs and suppression history. Quarantine records whose eligibility cannot be established instead of treating a Shopify phone field as an invitation to text. Have the destination team confirm the accepted import format and sending eligibility for the markets you serve before activating a segment.</p>
        <h2>Retain Loyalty without reviving messaging</h2>
        <p>Postscript’s <a href="https://help.postscript.io/en/articles/13564274-set-up-your-yotpo-integration">Yotpo integration guide</a> documents referencing reward points in SMS automations. That concerns retained rewards data; it is not proof that an inactive messaging account can export subscribers. Verify the correct product credentials and plan with the vendors. On a staff profile, compare the point value in the source with the rendered message, then change the source value and check the next evaluation. Keep a neutral branch for missing or stale points.</p>
        <h2>Reviews need a different handoff</h2>
        <p>Decide whether retained Yotpo Reviews sends its own requests or whether another supported route owns them. An order event alone is not evidence that the buyer has received or used a product. Test a delayed delivery, a cancelled order and an already-reviewed order before adding SMS reminders. Do not infer a Reviews connection or shared suppression merely because the Loyalty integration exists. Keep a list of review-request exclusions accessible to both channel owners.</p>
        <h2>A proposed keyword and reply rehearsal</h2>
        <p>Use staff records to trace a signup from each capture source through eligibility and into the intended welcome path. Check a repeat signup and a previously opted-out number. Then rehearse a reply that needs a human: product suitability, sizing or an order issue. Name the support queue and escalation owner, including what happens when nobody is monitoring replies. These are acceptance exercises, not results from a merchant test.</p>
        <h2>Drops and replenishment require separate stop rules</h2>
        <p>For a product drop, verify stock and recent-purchaser exclusion immediately before the send. For replenishment, derive a candidate interval from the relevant product and buying pattern; exclude gifts, subscriptions already fulfilling and unresolved service issues. A customer buying a gift is not necessarily consuming it. Keep promotional urgency separate from advice that requires support expertise. Do not select a vendor from an invented SMS revenue-share threshold.</p>
        <h2>Cost and cutover record</h2>
        <p>Request a current quote using eligible recipients, destination countries, message type, expected cadence, carrier-related charges and support needs. Include the separate email system and retained Reviews or Loyalty charges. Before enabling a new trigger, identify any surviving sender outside the retired service and pause its equivalent job. Record activation time, exclusions and a stop switch. If permission evidence is missing, restore capture for new eligible signups rather than loading the uncertain historic list.</p>
      </article>
      <nav class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related guides">
        <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo and Postscript</a>
        <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
